nkedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T09:05:04-07:00","id":988273,"title":"","content":"-Bale Hounds, Maeljin and other dark things<br /> <br /> -updated WAtP Shapeshifters<br /> <br /> -ancient Sumer setting<br /> <br /> -lost Firstborns and what they have done in the meantime<br /> <br /> -more &quot;city-settings&quot; and their like (because you can never have enough of those)<br /> <br /> -something about those spirits of distant stars and such alien things :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T08:48:03-07:00","id":991407,"title":"","content":"Same here for a Bale Hounds &amp; maeljin 2.0<br /> <br /> Changing Breeds 2.0, I know it was bad but I would love to see this as a supplement for W:tF.<br /> <br /> Elder &amp; high PU werewolves. I definitely want to see a book about this. With Dark Eras and this it would be a glorious chronicle to make. <br /> <br /> Lodges. I want to see more new or revised lodges from 1st ed. <br /> <br /> Setting book(s) like hunting grounds: the rockies, Shadows of the UK &amp; Mexico, and WoD Chicago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T13:10:55-07:00","id":991497,"title":"","content":"What I want... is a section about going to the Moon. Like physically going there. Possibly a &quot;moon base&quot; setting describing it.<br /> <br /> Most times Luna is physically distant... What if you could change that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 10-22-2016, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T06:13:48-07:00","id":991816,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a book in the same vein as Predators and Skinchangers. Prey is probably one of the most critical parts of Werewolf. Personally couldn't care less about bale hounds / maeljin myself, but this is where they'd be, along with alternative shifter types, expanded hosts, ridden and more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:23:19-07:00","id":992144,"title":"","content":"Ancient Summer setting.<br /> <br /> A book o Hosts, fully updating Azlu and Beshilu to 2nd Edition, and ofering other Hosts.<br /> <br /> A book o Claimed, updating their Predator Rules to 2nd edition and making them player characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T04:46:06-07:00","id":992329,"title":"","content":"A book that explains Influence in a definitive way and gives me examples of it.<br /> <br /> A book on the other shifters that could represent weird allies or worthy enemies.<br /> <br /> A book that makes the Pure as menacing as I feel they should be.<br /> <br /> A Mirror styles book that presents the Tribes as divisions of both philosophy AND origin, mimicking the varied origins of werewolves. A tribe of werewolves turned from being bitten, a tribe of werewolves born of from a family line, a tribe of werewolves born of wolves, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T13:26:19-07:00","id":994180,"title":"","content":"I can't even describe what I'd do for an entire book on WatP-style shifters. Especially if it threw in some hack ideas/possibilities for adapting the rest of the line to focus on more varieties of shifters, or incorporating them into packs. Speaking of, I've heard that The Pack has info on other supernatural beings as part of a werewolf pack, will there be anything on other shifters there?<br /> <br /> I love lists of stuff, so if you just gave me a long list of profiles and story information and stats of various shifter types, I'd be super happy.<br /> <br /> And while I definitely want WatP style shadow societies of shifters, some info on &quot;flukes&quot; might be nice, but I think that'll probably be handled by Deviant. <br /> <br /> On the topic of stuff for players, the only thing that I want for werewolf almost as much as more shifters would be playable Claimed and more stuff for playing mortal spiritualists.<br /> <br /> Other shifters are great because you don't even have to use them for werewolf, they make great localized miscellaneous weirdness to throw at other splats. Smaller, isolated shadow societies of shapeshifters are particularly good Hunter antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-27-2016, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T00:09:19-07:00","id":996476,"title":"","content":"There is something I've been curious about. In one of the Mirrors books, space opera is discussed some. but as has been pointed out some already... The possibilities of a werewolf actually first changing -on- the moon are interesting. But what about if they were outside the solar system in a grim, futuristic setting? I'd honestly like to see a grim future setting in Werewolf where the Forsaken have used Luna's initial aid to ally with other moons... And the resulting bizarre Forsaken with perhaps completely alien Auspices that follow. Are they still Luna's children? Are they still Forsaken? And what might the Pure do or react with at the possibility of having 'auspices' untainted by their most despised foe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T05:04:09-07:00","id":1064711,"title":"","content":"Blasphemies 2.0 and Predators 2.0 are sharing my top of the list, with Tribes/Signs of the Moon holding second place and The Pure on third place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T13:17:20-07:00","id":1064898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987283-if-you-could-get-any-book-or-section-in-wtf-what-would-you-want?p=991816#post991816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see a book in the same vein as Predators and Skinchangers. Prey is probably one of the most critical parts of Werewolf. Personally couldn't care less about bale hounds / maeljin myself, but this is where they'd be, along with alternative shifter types, expanded hosts, ridden and more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't remember whose idea this was, but it was for a set of five books, each about a tribe and its corresponding sacred prey. I wouldn't mind that (especially if it started with Hunters in Darkness and Hosts).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T05:18:41-07:00","id":1065197,"title":"","content":"Somewhat in the same vein of what you suggested but I would love to see a 'Sacred Prey' book for 2ED a Chapter devoted to each of them. Even better if this contains complete examples or ready to play adversaries for the Storytellers that are pushed for time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7354-monsieurcutts","name":"MonsieurCutts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7354_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T20:05:31-07:00","id":1065557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a hre